Amethyst UniXNU Partitioner - @ZIP_MODE@ ZIP
=============================================

This ZIP contains a statically linked AArch64 helper (bin/partitioner) and a
small recovery shell entry point. It never downloads anything.

Read the project README and docs/HARDWARE-TEST-REPORT.md before using it.
The project has NOT been validated on Amethyst hardware.

Requests
  Everything lives on the USB OTG stick, mounted at /usb_otg. The installer
  refuses to run if /usb_otg is absent rather than falling back to /sdcard.
  samples/request-plan.conf and samples/request-apply.conf in this ZIP are
  templates. Copy the appropriate one to
      /usb_otg/Amethyst-UniXNU-Partitioner/request.conf
  and replace every placeholder. (In the project repository these templates
  live under examples/, but inside this ZIP they are packaged as samples/.)

Inspect ZIP
  Reads the current state and writes inspect-*.txt and inspect-*.json under
  /usb_otg/Amethyst-UniXNU-Partitioner/. It performs no partition or filesystem
  writes, even when it reports UNSUPPORTED.

Plan ZIP
  Requires /usb_otg/Amethyst-UniXNU-Partitioner/request.conf with:
      mode = plan
      size_gib = <size>
      plan_dir = <absolute directory>
  It reads the device, GPT and mounted F2FS and writes a plan bundle. It does
  not resize anything.

Apply ZIP
  Requires /usb_otg/Amethyst-UniXNU-Partitioner/request.conf with:
      mode = apply
      plan = <bundle directory>
      confirm = unixnu <plan_id> <serial> <unixnu_bytes>
      acknowledge_data_loss = yes
  The bundle must be on the USB OTG stick (or /tmp), never on /sdcard or
  /data, because apply unmounts /data and /sdcard is a bind mount of it.
  The helper revalidates every identity, GPT byte, F2FS field and metadata
  hash before its first destructive operation.

  After rebooting recovery you can reuse this ZIP in read-only modes:
      mode = verify   (plan = ...)
      mode = recover  (plan = ...)

WARNING
  Shrinking F2FS moves file data. A GPT backup does not contain file contents,
  and restoring an old GPT cannot undo an F2FS shrink. Keep an independent
  userdata/metadata backup. There is no automatic retry or rollback.
